From: originaxiom <originaxiom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:32:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 12;
 first built on 5c7abd72a; built again on main's bf76e5ab1 with the 41 patches
 of R80b, the ten patches of series 4, the move of the old front pages and the
 first eleven of series 5 applied): WHAT KEEPS A TEST FROM RUNNING IS READ
 WHEREVER IT STANDS (main's M13, its third item, the first part). Two readers
 ask whether a test can be kept from running: the reader of a gate's control,
 and the reader that holds the tests of every lock to what they were. Both
 read the first level of statements of the file: a mark on the module, or a
 call that skips, each written as a statement of its own. Main's case: a
 control whose module skips itself at import under a condition, or in an
 except clause, passed the controls gate. FOUND WHILE BUILDING IT, and of the
 same kind: a call to importorskip given to a name, which is how most modules
 write it; a skip that is raised; a mark bound to a name, or made by a
 function of the module, and put on the test by that name; a mark that a class
 sets in its own body; a fixture of the module that skips the test that asks
 for it, by a parameter or by a mark, or that every test gets unasked; and,
 for a control, a module that tells the collector it holds no test. THE MEND:
 the whole first level of the module is read: every statement that runs as the
 module is loaded, which is all of it but what stands inside a function, a
 lambda or a class. A test is read with the marks it wears by a name of the
 module and with the module's fixtures that it asks for. One reader, in the
 vacuity checker, serves both, so that the two agree. ON MAIN: of 1,626 locks
 the reader as it was and the reader of this patch give the same table for
 1,593. In 32 the module's own switches are more, 23 of them an importorskip
 given to a name. In two files fifteen tests have more of their own: a mark
 worn by a name, and a fixture that skips. Nowhere does the new reader count
 less. None of the 53 controls is kept from running, by the wider reading as
 by the old. No lock gained a switch since the rule's anchor that only the
 wider reader sees, so the rule on tests that are switched off reads at main's
 head as it did. WHAT THIS CHANGES IS WHAT IS READ, NOT WHAT IS ASKED: a lock
 is held to what it was when the rule came, and both days are read by the same
 reader, so a module that skips where a package is missing owes no record for
 it. WHAT IT DOES NOT REACH: a skip decided outside the lock's own file, in a
 conftest or in the options the suite is run with; a test kept from running by
 a condition in its own body that names no skip; a name for a mark that the
 module takes from another module. The lock: one test added to
 tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py, thirteen shapes and five twins;
 two added to tests/test_nothing_leaves_a_ledger.py, eleven shapes and two
 twins, and a class marked in its body. On the commit before, all three fail:
 the controls gate passes on a control whose module skips under a condition;
 the vacuity gate passes on a lock switched off the same way; and a class's
 own mark is not counted. Tested against planted errors; reproduced, main's
 two shapes; computed once. 0 of 19.

